<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Santones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Mediolanum Santonum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Saintonge on the Atlantic coast, whose land was the goal of the Helvetian migration of 58 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Santones lived north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gironde-estuary">Gironde estuary</a>, along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charente">Charente</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charente-maritime">Charente-Maritime</a>. Caesar records that the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetii">Helvetii</a> planned to settle in their land, which alarmed him because it lay close to the Roman Province.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their coast gave them ships and seamen, which Caesar requisitioned in 56 BCE for the war against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a>. They struck coins in large numbers and traded salt and goods along the Atlantic.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They joined the revolt of 52 BCE with twelve thousand men. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintes">Mediolanum Santonum</a> (Saintes) became the first capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arch-of-germanicus">Arch of Germanicus</a> and a large amphitheatre. The region kept their name as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintonge">Saintonge</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/santones.jpg" alt="Santones" width="320" height="324"><figcaption>Image: World Imaging (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santones_gold_coin_5_to_1st_century_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mediolanum Santonum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=santones" aria-label="Santones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4665 566 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Santones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4985 822L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4985 822h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4985 822h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mediolanum Santonum. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=santones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

